note Allen voice generator: emits public/js/allen-voice.js on fd 1.
note The script is speech typing into Allen's message box and, when the visitor
note turns it on, replies read aloud by the browser's speech synthesis.
note ~N~ tokens in the js texts expand field N of vcfg, in order:
note 0 mic button id, 1 privacy note id, 2 read-aloud toggle id, 3 voice status
note id, 4 message box id, 5 local storage key for the read-aloud choice,
note 6 most characters read aloud per reply, 7 characters per utterance,
note 8 to 34 the visible sentences: 8 online recognition, 9 on-device recognition,
note 10 no recognition, 11 not a secure page, 12 start label, 13 stop label,
note 14 starting, 15 listening, 16 done, 17 nothing heard, 18 cancelled,
note 19 microphone blocked, 20 no microphone, 21 network, 22 language, 23 other
note error, 24 on-device fell back to online, 25 page hidden, 26 visitor typed,
note 27 no speech synthesis, 28 reading on, 29 reading off, 30 no on-device voice,
note 31 the label before Drake's own messages, 32 code skipped, 33 link, 34 rest.
note Allen's server transcription (POST raw audio, contract from the gateway):
note 35 presence path, whose JSON field transcribe is true only when the gateway
note runs the pinned recognizer; 36 transcribe path; 37 most clip bytes; 38 most
note clip milliseconds; 39 fewest clip milliseconds; 40 WAV sample rate in hertz.
note 41 to 53 sentences: 41 server privacy note (the gateway's own wording),
note 42 recording, 43 sending, 44 too short, 45 too long, 46 format refused,
note 47 no words in the clip, 48 rate limited, 49 retry lead, 50 busy, 51 the
note offer to use the browser's speech service instead, 52 switched, 53 server
note unreachable. 54 the spoken form of the name Aien (said like Ian): read
note aloud only, never displayed.
note vcheck refuses the table before anything is written: ids 0 to 5 are
note lowercase letters, digits and hyphens; 6, 7 and 37 to 40 are decimal digits;
note 35 and 36 are paths of lowercase letters, hyphens and slashes; 8 to 34 and
note 41 to 54 never hold a double quote, a backslash or a newline, because the js
note texts put them in double-quoted strings. raw refuses an em or en dash anywhere
note in the output (UTF-8 E2 80 94 and E2 80 93). The sentences are the site's
note copy: first person singular, Drake's voice; the assistant is named Aien
note (renamed from Allen, 2026-10-26), never "I". Internal ids and paths keep allen.
note Source language checked at omega-mv 55f9b0af47de70a3d06357985cf99ae3e45c016f.
text vcfg "allen-mic|allen-voice-privacy|allen-speak|allen-voice-status|allen-input|allen-voice-speak|4000|200|Voice typing uses your browser's online speech service: in Chrome your audio goes to Google's servers to become text, and other browsers may send it to their maker. My site never receives your audio, only the words you choose to send.|Voice typing runs on this device: your browser turns speech into text here and your audio does not leave it. Only the words you choose to send reach Aien.|Voice typing isn't available in this browser. You can still type your message.|Voice typing needs the secure https page. You can still type your message.|Start voice typing|Stop voice typing|Starting. Your browser may ask to use the microphone.|Listening. Speak, then tap the microphone again to stop, or press Escape to cancel.|Done. Your words are in the message box: check them, then press Send.|No words came through. Tap the microphone to try again.|Cancelled. The message box is back as it was.|The microphone is blocked for this site. Allow it in your browser's site settings, or type instead.|No microphone was found. You can type instead.|Your browser's speech service could not be reached. Check your connection, or type instead.|Voice typing doesn't support this page's language in your browser.|Voice typing stopped with an error. You can type instead.|On-device voice typing isn't ready in this browser, so it would use the online speech service. Read the privacy note, then tap the microphone again if that's fine.|Voice typing stopped because the page went to the background.|Voice typing stopped because you started typing.|Reading replies aloud isn't available in this browser.|Aien's replies will be read aloud by your browser's voice.|Replies are no longer read aloud.|Your browser lists no on-device voice for this language, so it may send reply text to its online voice service.|Drake wrote:|(code block skipped)|link|The rest is on the screen.|/allen/api/presence|/allen/api/transcribe|1048576|15000|300|16000|Voice typing records only after you tap the microphone, for up to 15 seconds. Your clip is sent to Aien's server, turned into text, and never saved: it stays in memory only and is discarded as soon as the text comes back. The text is shown to you; it is not logged.|Recording. Tap the microphone again when you finish, or press Escape to cancel.|Turning your words into text.|That clip was too short. Tap the microphone and speak a little longer.|That clip was too long for Aien's server. Try a shorter one.|Aien's server could not read this browser's audio format.|Aien's server could not make out any words in that clip.|Aien's server is taking too many clips right now.|Try again in|Aien's server is busy right now. Try again in a moment.|Use your browser's speech service instead|Switched to your browser's speech service. Read the privacy note, then tap the microphone if that's fine.|Aien's server could not be reached. Check your connection, or type instead.|Ian|"
const VFIELDS ulong 55
global output uchar 65536
global used ulong 1
global marker ulong 2
global tail uchar 2

fn flush to void
p = ulong 0
while lt p get used 0 bound 65536
n = write 1 output p sub get used 0 p
if le n 0
trap 3
end
p = add p ulong n
end
put used 0 0
end

note raw: one output byte; trap 12 completes an em or en dash.
fn raw c uchar to void
if or eq c 147 eq c 148
if eq get tail 1 128
if eq get tail 0 226
trap 12
end
end
end
put tail 0 get tail 1
put tail 1 c
if eq get used 0 len output
flush
end
put output get used 0 c
put used 0 add get used 0 1
end

note idbyte: a-z, 0-9 or hyphen. digit: 0-9. copybyte: not quote, backslash, newline.
fn idbyte c uchar to bool
if and ge c 97 le c 122
ret true
end
ret or digit c eq c 45
end

fn digit c uchar to bool
ret and ge c 48 le c 57
end

fn copybyte c uchar to bool
ret not or or eq c 34 eq c 92 eq c 10
end

note okbyte: whether c may stand in field k; trap 9 past the last field.
fn okbyte k ulong c uchar to bool
if le k 5
ret idbyte c
end
if le k 7
ret digit c
end
if le k 34
ret copybyte c
end
if le k 36
ret pathbyte c
end
if le k 40
ret digit c
end
if lt k VFIELDS
ret copybyte c
end
trap 9
end

note pathbyte: a-z, hyphen or slash.
fn pathbyte c uchar to bool
if and ge c 97 le c 122
ret true
end
ret or eq c 45 eq c 47
end

note vcheck: exactly VFIELDS pipe-terminated fields, none empty, each byte allowed.
fn vcheck to void
k = ulong 0
w = ulong 0
p = ulong 0
while lt p len vcfg
c = get vcfg p
if eq c 124
if eq w 0
trap 8
end
k = add k 1
w = 0
else
if not okbyte k c
trap 10
end
w = add w 1
end
p = add p 1
end
if ne k VFIELDS
trap 11
end
end

note field: the k-th pipe-terminated field of vcfg; a missing field traps.
fn field k ulong to void
p = ulong 0
i = ulong 0
while lt p len vcfg
c = get vcfg p
if eq c 124
if eq i k
ret
end
i = add i 1
else
if eq i k
raw c
end
end
p = add p 1
end
trap 3
end

note byteput: ~N~ expands field N; any other byte is copied.
fn byteput c uchar to void
if eq c 126
if eq get marker 0 0
put marker 0 1
put marker 1 0
else
field get marker 1
put marker 0 0
end
else
if eq get marker 0 1
if not digit c
trap 3
end
put marker 1 add mul get marker 1 10 ulong sub c 48
else
raw c
end
end
end

note JavaScript part 0
text js0 "/* Allen voice: speech typing into the message box, and replies read aloud.\n *\n * Generated by om/allen-voice/voice.om; never hand-edit. Element ids, limits\n * and every visible sentence come from the vcfg table in voice.om.\n *\n * Speech typing. The microphone is touched only after a tap on the mic\n * button: nothing here asks for it, or for any permission, when the page\n * loads. Recognized words go into the message box as editable text, with an\n * input event, and are never sent: the visitor presses Send. The privacy note\n * says where the audio goes before the first tap. Three engines, chosen\n * before any tap: the browser's on-device recognizer when it reports one\n * installed for the language (processLocally set; the audio stays here);\n * else Allen's server when the gateway's presence says transcribe is true\n * (one clip per tap, POSTed once, Safari's MP4 turned into 16 kHz WAV here);\n * else the browser's online speech service (Chrome sends audio to Google).\n * A server failure never retries elsewhere: the browser's recognition is\n * offered as a button, with its own note, and needs another tap.\n *\n * Replies read aloud. Off unless the visitor turns it on; the choice (on or\n * off, nothing else) is the only thing kept, in local storage. Uses the\n * browser's speech synthesis, never a recording of anyone. Allen's replies are\n * read as they are; a message Drake typed himself is read after the words\n * \"Drake wrote:\" so a synthetic voice is never taken for either of them.\n * Speech stops on a new request, a mic tap, turning it off, or when the page\n * is hidden. No transcript and no audio is stored or sent by this file.\n */\n(() => {\n  'use strict';\n  const byId = id => document.getElementById(id);\n  const input = byId('~4~');\n  const mic = byId('~0~');\n  const privacy = byId('~1~');\n"

note JavaScript part 1
text js1 "  const toggle = byId('~2~');\n  if (!input || (!mic && !toggle)) return;\n  const STORE = '~5~';\n  const SPEAK_MAX = ~6~;\n  const CHUNK = ~7~;\n  const PRESENCE = '~35~';\n  const ENDPOINT = '~36~';\n  const MAX_BYTES = ~37~;\n  const MAX_MS = ~38~;\n  const MIN_MS = ~39~;\n  const RATE = ~40~;\n  const COPY = Object.freeze({\n    cloud: \"~8~\",\n    local: \"~9~\",\n    none: \"~10~\",\n    insecure: \"~11~\",\n    start: \"~12~\",\n    stop: \"~13~\",\n    starting: \"~14~\",\n    listening: \"~15~\",\n    done: \"~16~\",\n    nothing: \"~17~\",\n    cancelled: \"~18~\",\n    blocked: \"~19~\",\n    nomic: \"~20~\",\n    network: \"~21~\",\n    lang: \"~22~\",\n    failed: \"~23~\",\n    fallback: \"~24~\",\n    hidden: \"~25~\",\n    typed: \"~26~\",\n    noSpeak: \"~27~\",\n    speakOn: \"~28~\",\n    speakOff: \"~29~\",\n    remote: \"~30~\",\n    drake: \"~31~\",\n    code: \"~32~\",\n    link: \"~33~\",\n    rest: \"~34~\",\n    server: \"~41~\",\n    recording: \"~42~\",\n    sending: \"~43~\",\n    short: \"~44~\",\n    toolong: \"~45~\",\n    format: \"~46~\",\n    unclear: \"~47~\",\n    rate: \"~48~\",\n    retry: \"~49~\",\n    busy: \"~50~\",\n    offer: \"~51~\",\n    switched: \"~52~\",\n    serverdown: \"~53~\",\n  });\n\n  function lang() {\n    const page = document.documentElement && document.documentElement.lang;\n    const nav = window.navigator && window.navigator.language;\n    return String(page || nav || 'en-US');\n  }\n\n  /* One live region for both halves; made here when the page has none. */\n  let status = byId('~3~');\n  if (!status) {\n    status = document.createElement('p');\n    status.id = '~3~';\n    status.className = 'allen-voice-status';\n    const after = privacy || mic || toggle;\n    if (after.parentNode) after.parentNode.insertBefore(status, after.nextSibling);\n  }\n  status.setAttribute('role', 'status');\n  status.setAttribute('aria-live', 'polite');\n  function say(text) {\n    if (status.textContent !== text) status.textContent = text;\n  }\n\n"

note JavaScript part 2
text js2 "  /* Speech typing. */\n  const Recognition = typeof window.SpeechRecognition === 'function' ? window.SpeechRecognition\n    : typeof window.webkitSpeechRecognition === 'function' ? window.webkitSpeechRecognition : null;\n  const secure = window.isSecureContext === true;\n  const canLocal = !!Recognition && Recognition === window.SpeechRecognition\n    && typeof Recognition.available === 'function' && 'processLocally' in Recognition.prototype;\n  let mode = !Recognition ? 'none' : !secure ? 'insecure' : 'cloud';\n  let browserMode = mode;\n  let rec = null;\n  let clip = null;\n  let state = 'idle';\n  let base = '';\n  let wrote = null;\n  let writing = false;\n  let heard = false;\n  let ending = '';\n\n  function showPrivacy() {\n    if (privacy) privacy.textContent = COPY[mode];\n    if (!mic) return;\n    const off = mode === 'none' || mode === 'insecure';\n    mic.disabled = off;\n    mic.setAttribute('aria-disabled', off ? 'true' : 'false');\n    mic.dataset.voice = mode;\n    const described = [privacy && privacy.id, status.id].filter(Boolean).join(' ');\n    if (described) mic.setAttribute('aria-describedby', described);\n  }\n  function setState(next, message) {\n    state = next;\n    if (mic) {\n      const live = next !== 'idle';\n      mic.dataset.state = next;\n      mic.setAttribute('aria-pressed', live ? 'true' : 'false');\n      mic.setAttribute('aria-label', live ? COPY.stop : COPY.start);\n      mic.title = live ? COPY.stop : COPY.start;\n    }\n    if (message !== undefined) say(message);\n  }\n\n  /* Only an installed on-device recognizer counts as on device. */\n  async function probeLocal() {\n    if (!canLocal || mode !== 'cloud') return false;\n    try {\n      return (await Recognition.available({ langs: [lang()], processLocally: true })) === 'available';\n    } catch (_) {\n      return false;\n    }\n  }\n"

note JavaScript part 3
text js3 "  /* Allen's server is used only when the gateway's presence says transcribe is\n     true and this browser can record after a tap; nothing is recorded to find\n     out. An absent or false field keeps the browser's own recognition. */\n  function canRecord() {\n    const media = window.navigator && window.navigator.mediaDevices;\n    return secure && !!media && typeof media.getUserMedia === 'function' && typeof window.MediaRecorder === 'function'\n      && (!!opusType() || typeof (window.AudioContext || window.webkitAudioContext) === 'function');\n  }\n  async function probeServer() {\n    if (!canRecord() || typeof window.fetch !== 'function') return false;\n    try {\n      const response = await window.fetch(PRESENCE, { cache: 'no-store', credentials: 'omit', headers: { Accept: 'application/json' } });\n      const reply = response.ok ? await response.json() : null;\n      return !!reply && typeof reply === 'object' && reply.transcribe === true;\n    } catch (_) {\n      return false;\n    }\n  }\n  /* On device first (the audio stays here), then Allen's server, then the\n     browser's online service. Decided once, before any tap is needed. */\n  async function probe() {\n    const [local, server] = await Promise.all([probeLocal(), probeServer()]);\n    if (rec || clip || state !== 'idle') return;\n    if (local) browserMode = 'local';\n    const next = local ? 'local' : server ? 'server' : mode;\n    if (next === mode) return;\n    mode = next;\n    showPrivacy();\n    say('');\n  }\n\n  function joined(text) {\n    const said = String(text).replace(/\\s+/g, ' ').trim();\n    if (!said) return base;\n    const gap = base && !/\\s$/.test(base) ? ' ' : '';\n    let value = base + gap + said;\n    const max = input.maxLength;\n    if (max > 0 && value.length > max) value = value.slice(0, max);\n    return value;\n  }\n"

note JavaScript part 4
text js4 "  function write(value) {\n    if (input.value === value) return;\n    writing = true;\n    input.value = value;\n    wrote = value;\n    try {\n      input.setSelectionRange(value.length, value.length);\n    } catch (_) {\n      /* Some input types have no selection. */\n    }\n    input.dispatchEvent(new Event('input', { bubbles: true }));\n    writing = false;\n  }\n\n  const ERRORS = Object.freeze({\n    'not-allowed': 'blocked',\n    'service-not-allowed': 'blocked',\n    'audio-capture': 'nomic',\n    network: 'network',\n    'language-not-supported': 'lang',\n    'no-speech': 'nothing',\n  });\n\n  function startBrowser() {\n    if (!Recognition || (mode !== 'cloud' && mode !== 'local') || rec) return;\n    stopSpeaking();\n    const r = new Recognition();\n    r.lang = lang();\n    r.continuous = false;\n    r.interimResults = true;\n    r.maxAlternatives = 1;\n    if (mode === 'local') r.processLocally = true;\n    base = input.value;\n    wrote = null;\n    heard = false;\n    ending = '';\n    r.onaudiostart = () => {\n      if (rec === r && state === 'starting') setState('listening', COPY.listening);\n    };\n    r.onstart = r.onaudiostart;\n    r.onresult = event => {\n      if (rec !== r || ending) return;\n      let text = '';\n      for (let i = 0; i < event.results.length; i += 1) {\n        const best = event.results[i] && event.results[i][0];\n        if (best && typeof best.transcript === 'string') text += best.transcript;\n      }\n      if (text.trim()) heard = true;\n      write(joined(text));\n    };\n    r.onerror = event => {\n      if (rec !== r) return;\n      const code = event && typeof event.error === 'string' ? event.error : '';\n      if (code === 'aborted') return;\n      if (mode === 'local' && (code === 'language-not-supported' || code === 'service-not-allowed')) {\n        mode = 'cloud';\n        browserMode = 'cloud';\n        showPrivacy();\n        ending = ending || 'fallback';\n        return;\n      }\n      ending = ending || ERRORS[code] || 'failed';\n    };\n    r.onend = () => {\n      if (rec !== r) return;\n      rec = null;\n      if (ending === 'cancelled') write(base);\n      const said = ending ? COPY[ending] : heard ? COPY.done : COPY.nothing;\n      setState('idle', said);\n    };\n    rec = r;\n    setState('starting', COPY.starting);\n    try {\n      r.start();\n    } catch (_) {\n      rec = null;\n      setState('idle', COPY.failed);\n    }\n  }\n"

note JavaScript part 5
text js5 "  function stop() {\n    if (!rec) return;\n    if (state === 'stopping') {\n      rec.abort();\n      return;\n    }\n    setState('stopping');\n    rec.stop();\n  }\n  function end(why) {\n    if (clip) {\n      dropClip(why);\n      return;\n    }\n    if (!rec) return;\n    ending = why;\n    setState('stopping');\n    rec.abort();\n  }\n\n  /* Allen's server. One clip per tap, recorded only between the taps, held in\n     memory, sent once to ENDPOINT and never anywhere else. A refused or failed\n     clip is dropped; the browser's own recognition is only offered, as a\n     button, and the visitor has to tap the microphone again after reading\n     its privacy note. */\n  function opusType() {\n    const MR = window.MediaRecorder;\n    if (typeof MR !== 'function' || typeof MR.isTypeSupported !== 'function') return '';\n    for (const type of ['audio/webm;codecs=opus', 'audio/ogg;codecs=opus']) {\n      try {\n        if (MR.isTypeSupported(type)) return type;\n      } catch (_) {\n        /* Try the next type. */\n      }\n    }\n    return '';\n  }\n  function now() {\n    return window.performance && typeof window.performance.now === 'function' ? window.performance.now() : Date.now();\n  }\n  function release(c) {\n    if (c.timer) window.clearTimeout(c.timer);\n    c.timer = 0;\n    if (c.stream) {\n      for (const track of c.stream.getTracks()) track.stop();\n    }\n    c.stream = null;\n  }\n  function dropClip(why) {\n    const c = clip;\n    clip = null;\n    c.dropped = true;\n    if (c.controller) c.controller.abort();\n    if (c.recorder && c.recorder.state !== 'inactive') {\n      try {\n        c.recorder.stop();\n      } catch (_) {\n        /* Already stopped. */\n      }\n    }\n    release(c);\n    c.chunks = [];\n    setState('idle', COPY[why] || COPY.cancelled);\n  }\n  function done(c, said) {\n    if (clip === c) clip = null;\n    setState('idle', said);\n  }\n"

note JavaScript part 6
text js6 "  async function startServer() {\n    stopSpeaking();\n    const c = { stream: null, recorder: null, chunks: [], mime: '', began: 0, ms: 0, timer: 0, controller: null, dropped: false };\n    clip = c;\n    hideOffer();\n    setState('starting', COPY.starting);\n    let stream = null;\n    try {\n      stream = await window.navigator.mediaDevices.getUserMedia({ audio: { channelCount: 1, echoCancellation: true, noiseSuppression: true } });\n    } catch (error) {\n      if (clip !== c) return;\n      const name = error && error.name;\n      done(c, name === 'NotAllowedError' || name === 'SecurityError' ? COPY.blocked : name === 'NotFoundError' || name === 'OverconstrainedError' ? COPY.nomic : COPY.failed);\n      return;\n    }\n    c.stream = stream;\n    if (clip !== c) {\n      release(c);\n      return;\n    }\n    c.mime = opusType();\n    try {\n      c.recorder = c.mime ? new window.MediaRecorder(stream, { mimeType: c.mime, audioBitsPerSecond: 32000 }) : new window.MediaRecorder(stream);\n      c.recorder.ondataavailable = event => {\n        if (event.data && event.data.size) c.chunks.push(event.data);\n      };\n      c.recorder.onstop = () => {\n        finishClip(c);\n      };\n      c.recorder.start();\n    } catch (_) {\n      release(c);\n      done(c, COPY.failed);\n      return;\n    }\n    c.began = now();\n    c.timer = window.setTimeout(() => {\n      if (clip === c && state === 'listening') stopClip();\n    }, MAX_MS);\n    setState('listening', COPY.recording);\n  }\n  function stopClip() {\n    const c = clip;\n    if (!c || !c.recorder) return;\n    c.ms = now() - c.began;\n    setState('sending', COPY.sending);\n    try {\n      c.recorder.stop();\n    } catch (_) {\n      release(c);\n      done(c, COPY.failed);\n    }\n  }\n  async function finishClip(c) {\n    release(c);\n    if (clip !== c || c.dropped) return;\n    const type = c.mime || (c.chunks[0] && c.chunks[0].type) || '';\n    const recorded = new Blob(c.chunks, { type });\n    c.chunks = [];\n    if (c.ms < MIN_MS || !recorded.size) {\n      done(c, COPY.short);\n      return;\n    }\n    let body = recorded;\n    let sent = c.mime;\n    if (!sent) {\n      let samples = null;\n      try {\n        samples = await decodeMono(recorded);\n      } catch (_) {\n        samples = null;\n      }\n      if (clip !== c) return;\n      if (!samples) {\n        done(c, COPY.format);\n        return;\n      }\n      const pcm = resample(samples.data, samples.rate);\n      if (pcm.length * 1000 < MIN_MS * RATE) {\n        done(c, COPY.short);\n        return;\n      }\n      body = new Blob([wav(pcm)], { type: 'audio/wav' });\n      sent = 'audio/wav';\n    }\n    if (body.size > MAX_BYTES) {\n      done(c, COPY.toolong);\n      return;\n    }\n    upload(c, body, sent);\n  }\n"

note JavaScript part 7
text js7 "  async function upload(c, body, type) {\n    c.controller = new AbortController();\n    let response = null;\n    let reply = null;\n    try {\n      response = await window.fetch(ENDPOINT, { method: 'POST', headers: { 'Content-Type': type, Accept: 'application/json' }, body, cache: 'no-store', credentials: 'omit', signal: c.controller.signal });\n      reply = await response.json().catch(() => null);\n    } catch (_) {\n      if (clip !== c) return;\n      offerBrowser();\n      done(c, COPY.serverdown);\n      return;\n    }\n    if (clip !== c) return;\n    if (response.ok && reply && typeof reply.text === 'string') {\n      const said = reply.text.trim();\n      if (!said) {\n        done(c, COPY.unclear);\n        return;\n      }\n      base = input.value;\n      write(joined(said));\n      done(c, COPY.done);\n      return;\n    }\n    offerBrowser();\n    done(c, refused(response, reply));\n  }\n  function refused(response, reply) {\n    const code = response.status;\n    if (code === 413) return COPY.toolong;\n    if (code === 415) return COPY.format;\n    if (code === 422) return COPY.unclear;\n    if (code === 503) return COPY.busy;\n    if (code === 429) {\n      const header = Number.parseInt(response.headers && response.headers.get ? response.headers.get('Retry-After') || '' : '', 10);\n      const field = reply && Number.isSafeInteger(reply.retry_after) ? reply.retry_after : NaN;\n      const wait = Number.isSafeInteger(header) && header > 0 ? header : field > 0 ? field : 0;\n      return wait && wait <= 3600 ? `${COPY.rate} ${COPY.retry} ${wait} s.` : COPY.rate;\n    }\n    return COPY.failed;\n  }\n\n  /* Safari records only AAC in MP4, which the gateway refuses: the clip is\n     decoded here, mixed to mono, resampled to RATE and sent as 16-bit PCM WAV. */\n  function decodeMono(blob) {\n    const Ctx = window.AudioContext || window.webkitAudioContext;\n    if (typeof Ctx !== 'function') return Promise.reject(new Error('no audio context'));\n    return blob.arrayBuffer().then(data => {\n      const ctx = new Ctx();\n      const closed = () => {\n        if (typeof ctx.close === 'function') ctx.close().catch(() => {});\n      };\n      return new Promise((ok, bad) => {\n        const pending = ctx.decodeAudioData(data, ok, bad);\n        if (pending && typeof pending.then === 'function') pending.then(ok, bad);\n      }).then(buffer => {\n        closed();\n        const channels = Math.max(1, buffer.numberOfChannels | 0);\n        const out = new Float32Array(buffer.length);\n        for (let ch = 0; ch < channels; ch += 1) {\n          const part = buffer.getChannelData(ch);\n          for (let i = 0; i < out.length; i += 1) out[i] += part[i] / channels;\n        }\n        return { data: out, rate: buffer.sampleRate };\n      }, error => {\n        closed();\n        throw error;\n      });\n    });\n  }\n"

note JavaScript part 8
text js8 "  /* Down: each output sample is the mean of the input span it covers (a box\n     filter weighted by overlap). Up: linear interpolation. */\n  function resample(data, rate) {\n    if (!(rate > 0) || rate === RATE) return Float32Array.from(data);\n    const ratio = rate / RATE;\n    const n = Math.floor(data.length / ratio);\n    const out = new Float32Array(n);\n    if (ratio < 1) {\n      for (let i = 0; i < n; i += 1) {\n        const at = i * ratio;\n        const k = Math.floor(at);\n        const next = k + 1 < data.length ? data[k + 1] : data[k];\n        out[i] = data[k] + (next - data[k]) * (at - k);\n      }\n      return out;\n    }\n    for (let i = 0; i < n; i += 1) {\n      const from = i * ratio;\n      const to = from + ratio;\n      let sum = 0;\n      for (let k = Math.floor(from); k < to && k < data.length; k += 1) {\n        sum += data[k] * (Math.min(to, k + 1) - Math.max(from, k));\n      }\n      out[i] = sum / ratio;\n    }\n    return out;\n  }\n  /* RIFF WAVE, PCM format 1, one channel, RATE hertz, 16 bits, little-endian;\n     samples clamped to -1..1, negative scaled by 32768, positive by 32767. */\n  function wav(samples) {\n    const bytes = samples.length * 2;\n    const view = new DataView(new ArrayBuffer(44 + bytes));\n    const tag = (at, text) => {\n      for (let i = 0; i < 4; i += 1) view.setUint8(at + i, text.charCodeAt(i));\n    };\n    tag(0, 'RIFF');\n    view.setUint32(4, 36 + bytes, true);\n    tag(8, 'WAVE');\n    tag(12, 'fmt ');\n    view.setUint32(16, 16, true);\n    view.setUint16(20, 1, true);\n    view.setUint16(22, 1, true);\n    view.setUint32(24, RATE, true);\n    view.setUint32(28, RATE * 2, true);\n    view.setUint16(32, 2, true);\n    view.setUint16(34, 16, true);\n    tag(36, 'data');\n    view.setUint32(40, bytes, true);\n    for (let i = 0; i < samples.length; i += 1) {\n      const s = Math.max(-1, Math.min(1, samples[i] || 0));\n      view.setInt16(44 + i * 2, s < 0 ? Math.round(s * 32768) : Math.round(s * 32767), true);\n    }\n    return view.buffer;\n  }\n\n"

note JavaScript part 9
text js9 "  /* The browser's own recognition, offered after Allen's server failed. */\n  let offer = null;\n  function offerBrowser() {\n    if (!Recognition || !secure || !mic) return;\n    if (!offer) {\n      offer = document.createElement('button');\n      offer.type = 'button';\n      offer.id = 'allen-voice-browser';\n      offer.className = 'allen-tool allen-voice-browser';\n      offer.textContent = COPY.offer;\n      offer.addEventListener('click', () => {\n        if (state !== 'idle') return;\n        mode = browserMode;\n        hideOffer();\n        showPrivacy();\n        say(COPY.switched);\n      });\n      if (status.parentNode) status.parentNode.insertBefore(offer, status.nextSibling);\n    }\n    offer.hidden = false;\n  }\n  function hideOffer() {\n    if (offer) offer.hidden = true;\n  }\n\n  if (mic) {\n    showPrivacy();\n    setState('idle');\n    if (mode === 'none' || mode === 'insecure') say(COPY[mode]);\n    mic.addEventListener('click', event => {\n      event.preventDefault();\n      if (state === 'idle') {\n        if (mode === 'server') startServer();\n        else startBrowser();\n      } else if (clip && state === 'listening') stopClip();\n      else if (clip) dropClip('cancelled');\n      else stop();\n    });\n    input.addEventListener('input', () => {\n      if (!writing && rec && input.value !== wrote) end('typed');\n    });\n    document.addEventListener('keydown', event => {\n      if (event.key !== 'Escape' || (!rec && !clip)) return;\n      event.preventDefault();\n      event.stopPropagation();\n      end('cancelled');\n    }, true);\n    probe();\n  }\n\n  /* Replies read aloud. */\n  const synth = window.speechSynthesis && typeof window.SpeechSynthesisUtterance === 'function' ? window.speechSynthesis : null;\n  const box = !!toggle && toggle.tagName === 'INPUT' && String(toggle.type).toLowerCase() === 'checkbox';\n"

note JavaScript part 10
text js10 "  let speaking = false;\n  let unlocked = false;\n  /* Aien is said like Ian: speech gets the spoken form, the screen keeps Aien. */\n  const SAYNAME = '~54~';\n\n  function stored() {\n    try {\n      return window.localStorage.getItem(STORE) === 'on';\n    } catch (_) {\n      return false;\n    }\n  }\n  function store(on) {\n    try {\n      if (on) window.localStorage.setItem(STORE, 'on');\n      else window.localStorage.removeItem(STORE);\n    } catch (_) {\n      /* The choice lasts for this page only. */\n    }\n  }\n  function showToggle() {\n    if (!toggle) return;\n    if (box) toggle.checked = speaking;\n    else toggle.setAttribute('aria-pressed', speaking ? 'true' : 'false');\n    toggle.dataset.state = speaking ? 'on' : 'off';\n  }\n  function stopSpeaking() {\n    if (synth) synth.cancel();\n  }\n  function voice() {\n    const want = lang().toLowerCase().replace(/_/g, '-');\n    const family = want.split('-')[0];\n    let list = [];\n    try {\n      list = Array.from(synth.getVoices() || []);\n    } catch (_) {\n      list = [];\n    }\n    const tag = v => String(v && v.lang || '').toLowerCase().replace(/_/g, '-');\n    const near = list.filter(v => v && v.localService === true && tag(v).split('-')[0] === family);\n    return near.find(v => tag(v) === want) || near[0] || null;\n  }\n  /* Code is skipped, links are named, markdown marks are dropped, and the\n     whole word Aien is spoken as SAYNAME. */\n  function plain(text) {\n    return String(text)\n      .replace(/```[\\s\\S]*?(```|$)/g, ` ${COPY.code} `)\n      .replace(/https?:\\/\\/\\S+/g, COPY.link)\n      .replace(/[`*_#>\\x7e]+/g, '')\n      .replace(/\\|/g, ' ')\n      .replace(/\\bAien\\b/g, SAYNAME)\n      .replace(/\\s+/g, ' ')\n      .trim();\n  }\n  function pieces(text) {\n    const out = [];\n    let line = '';\n    for (const part of text.match(/[^.!?]+[.!?]*\\s*|[.!?]+\\s*/g) || []) {\n      let rest = part;\n      while (rest.length > CHUNK) {\n        if (line) out.push(line.trim());\n        line = '';\n        out.push(rest.slice(0, CHUNK).trim());\n        rest = rest.slice(CHUNK);\n      }\n      if (line.length + rest.length > CHUNK) {\n        out.push(line.trim());\n        line = '';\n      }\n      line += rest;\n    }\n    if (line.trim()) out.push(line.trim());\n    return out.filter(Boolean);\n  }\n"

note JavaScript part 11
text js11 "  function read(text, lead) {\n    if (!speaking || !synth || document.hidden) return;\n    let said = plain(text);\n    if (!said) return;\n    if (said.length > SPEAK_MAX) said = `${said.slice(0, SPEAK_MAX)} ${COPY.rest}`;\n    stopSpeaking();\n    const chosen = voice();\n    for (const part of pieces(lead ? `${lead} ${said}` : said)) {\n      const utterance = new window.SpeechSynthesisUtterance(part);\n      utterance.lang = lang();\n      if (chosen) utterance.voice = chosen;\n      synth.speak(utterance);\n    }\n  }\n  /* iOS speaks later only after one utterance inside a tap. */\n  function unlock() {\n    if (unlocked || !speaking || !synth) return;\n    unlocked = true;\n    const utterance = new window.SpeechSynthesisUtterance('');\n    utterance.volume = 0;\n    synth.speak(utterance);\n  }\n  function setSpeaking(on) {\n    speaking = !!on && !!synth;\n    store(speaking);\n    showToggle();\n    if (!speaking) {\n      stopSpeaking();\n      say(COPY.speakOff);\n      return;\n    }\n    unlock();\n    say(voice() ? COPY.speakOn : `${COPY.speakOn} ${COPY.remote}`);\n  }\n\n  if (toggle) {\n    if (!synth) {\n      toggle.disabled = true;\n      toggle.setAttribute('aria-disabled', 'true');\n      toggle.title = COPY.noSpeak;\n      speaking = false;\n    } else {\n      speaking = stored();\n    }\n    showToggle();\n    toggle.addEventListener(box ? 'change' : 'click', () => {\n      if (!synth) return;\n      setSpeaking(box ? toggle.checked : !speaking);\n    });\n  }\n\n  function hidden() {\n    if (!document.hidden) return;\n    stopSpeaking();\n    end('hidden');\n  }\n  document.addEventListener('visibilitychange', hidden);\n  window.addEventListener('pagehide', () => {\n    stopSpeaking();\n    end('hidden');\n  });\n\n  /* The chat transport (window.allen v1): a new request silences speech;\n     replies are read only when the visitor turned reading on. */\n"

note JavaScript part 12
text js12 "  let hooked = false;\n  function hook() {\n    const allen = window.allen;\n    if (hooked || !allen || typeof allen.on !== 'function') return;\n    hooked = true;\n    allen.on('send', () => {\n      stopSpeaking();\n      unlock();\n    });\n    allen.on('reply', detail => {\n      if (!detail || typeof detail.text !== 'string') return;\n      if (detail.outcome === 'Stopped.') return;\n      read(detail.text, '');\n    });\n    allen.on('human', detail => {\n      if (detail && typeof detail.text === 'string') read(detail.text, COPY.drake);\n    });\n  }\n  hook();\n  document.addEventListener('allen-ready', hook);\n\n  window.AllenVoice = Object.freeze({\n    version: 1,\n    mode: () => mode,\n    state: () => state,\n    speaking: () => speaking,\n  });\n})();\n"

